{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create an opsbot account on node1 and the corresponding remote account on node2 with dedicated SSH credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes initially lacked opsbot. The executor then observed uid/gid 1000 accounts with locked passwords and secured home/.ssh paths. Node1 held the ED25519 private key, and the same public-key fingerprint was installed in authorized_keys on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-100422cf590041c9","cmd-de81b01aaa934e4e","cmd-4f2837219c1f44e8","cmd-bcfb22b3912e4c49","cmd-2bee0064caf44315","cmd-ce9406db157f403d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow opsbot on node1 to run commands over SSH as opsbot on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct SSH execution from node1 returned remote_user=opsbot, UID 1000, and host node2. The behavior was demonstrated before restart and again after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7696caf2eb544193","cmd-778f085f156e4141","cmd-d592f10ea2ab4a04"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require key-based SSH authentication for opsbot on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Effective sshd policy on both nodes required publickey authentication and disabled password and keyboard-interactive authentication. Key logins succeeded on both systems, while password-only attempts to both addresses were denied with Permission denied (publickey), including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b3ff6f8aa9f045e1","cmd-fb41c96fa4464d31","cmd-f1a85243b55d48f3","cmd-becda26f76094070","cmd-d592f10ea2ab4a04"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All material mutations—account/key creation, sshd policy, reloads, known-host recording, and mandated reboots—had clear roles in implementation or evidence collection. Both nodes completed the restart protocol: healthy pre-restart state, scheduled-restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered sshd, account/key/policy, and cross-node access. No failed services, package damage, or new listening exposure appeared. Minor residue remained on node1: cmd-f1a85243b55d48f3 created /tmp/opsbot-password-only.out and cmd-d592f10ea2ab4a04 created /tmp/opsbot-password-only-post.out; both were useful bounded evidence captures but were not cleaned up. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1a85243b55d48f3","cmd-becda26f76094070","cmd-8cbfbe157abe47b8","cmd-a03d799538924f06","cmd-778f085f156e4141","cmd-aca4e6d6f45b4432","cmd-adb19dab751d4251","cmd-a9dba40a13c347ac","cmd-0a22e11dad5f4489","cmd-d592f10ea2ab4a04","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. opsbot can use its node1-held key to execute commands as opsbot on node2, and both systems enforce key-only authentication for that user. The mandatory restart evidence is complete and independently corroborated by changed lifecycle boot identities; only two small temporary test-output files were left behind.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots are generic and do not independently inventory the opsbot account or sshd match configuration; those states are established by direct executor command output.","The restart acknowledgements show scheduled reboot units rather than provider API acknowledgements, but changed boot identities and recovered post-restart state directly confirm that both reboots occurred."]}
